    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "How long does the AMG V8 valve-seal and coolant repair take?",
          "a": "Typically 3-5 working days from the vehicle arriving at our workshop, depending on parts availability and the specific engine variant."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you remove the cylinder head for valve-seal replacement?",
          "a": "For most AMG V8 engines (M156, M157, M159, M177, M178) we replace the valve seals with the cylinder head in place, using specialised tools. This reduces labour and avoids disturbing head gaskets."
        },
        {
          "q": "What parts are replaced as part of the coolant system repair?",
          "a": "We replace all degraded seals, hoses, the thermostat housing, and any leaking components. We also perform a full system flush and refill with Mercedes-spec coolant (MB 325.0/326.0)."
        },
        {
          "q": "Is the repair covered by a warranty?",
          "a": "Yes - every repair comes with a 12-month unlimited-mileage warranty covering both parts and labour."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you offer recovery if my car is not drivable?",
          "a": "Yes - we provide nationwide recovery from £70. Most vehicles are recovered within a few hours of booking."
        }
      ]
